"[2510.04374] GDPval: Evaluating AI Model Performance on Real-World Economically Valuable Tasks (https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.04374)\nciteturn3156view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn3148view0\",\"id\":5}); Total lines: 164\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Machine Learning\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 5 Oct 2025]\nL9: # Title:GDPval: Evaluating AI Model Performance on Real-World Economically Valuable Tasks\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Tejal Patwardhan , cite6†Rachel Dias , cite7†Elizabeth Proehl , cite8†Grace Kim , cite9†Michele Wang , cite10†Olivia Watkins , cite11†Simón Posada Fishman , cite12†Marwan Aljubeh , cite13†Phoebe Thacker , cite14†Laurance Fauconnet , cite15†Natalie S. Kim , cite16†Patrick Chao , cite17†Samuel Miserendino , cite18†Gildas Chabot , cite19†David Li , cite20†Michael Sharman , cite21†Alexandra Barr , cite22†Amelia Glaese , cite23†Jerry Tworek L12: View a PDF of the paper titled GDPval: Evaluating AI Model Performance on Real-World Economically Valuable Tasks, by Tejal Patwardhan and 18 other authors\nL13: \nL14: cite24†View PDF cite25†HTML (experimental) L15: > Abstract:We introduce GDPval, a benchmark evaluating AI model capabilities on real-world economically valuable tasks. GDPval covers the majority of U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics Work Activities for 44 occupations across the top 9 sectors contributing to U.S. GDP (Gross Domestic Product). Tasks are constructed from the representative work of industry professionals with an average of 14 years of experience.\nL16: We find that frontier model performance on GDPval is improving roughly linearly over time, and that the current best frontier models are approaching industry experts in deliverable quality. We analyze the potential for frontier models, when paired with human oversight, to perform GDPval tasks cheaper and faster than unaided experts. We also demonstrate that increased reasoning effort, increased task context, and increased scaffolding improves model performance on GDPval.\nL17: Finally, we open-source a gold subset of 220 tasks and provide a public automated grading service at cite26†this http URL†evals.openai.com to facilitate future research in understanding real-world model capabilities.\nL18: Subjects:  | Machine Learning (cs.LG); Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI); Computers and Society (cs.CY)\nL19: Cite as:  | cite27†arXiv:2510.04374 [cs.LG]\nL20:    | (or cite28†arXiv:2510.04374v1 [cs.LG] for this version)\nL21:    | cite29†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2510.04374†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL22: ## Submission history\nL23: \nL24: From: Michele Wang [cite30†view email ]\nL25: [v1] Sun, 5 Oct 2025 21:36:43 UTC (13,990 KB)\nL26: \nL27: Full-text links:\nL28: \nL29: ## Access Paper:\nL30: \nL31: View a PDF of the paper titled GDPval: Evaluating AI Model Performance on Real-World Economically Valuable Tasks, by Tejal Patwardhan and 18 other authors\nL32: \nL33:   * cite24†View PDF L34:   * cite25†HTML (experimental) L35:   * cite31†TeX Source L36: \nL37: cite32†view license†creativecommons.org L38: ### Current browse context:\nL39: \nL40: cs.LG\nL41: \nL42: cite33†< prev |   cite34†next > L43: \nL44: cite35†new | cite36†recent | cite37†2025-10 L45: \nL46: Change to browse by:\nL47: \nL48: cite38†cs L49: cite39†cs.AI L50: cite40†cs.CY L51: \nL52: ### References & Citations\nL53: \nL54:   * cite41†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L55:   * cite42†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L56:   * cite43†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L57: \nL58: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL59: \nL60: ## BibTeX formatted